{"1852929874060878051":{"a":"<p>@DrGregLittle2 @lukecaverns Forests and swamps. Look for mounds or stepped squares which measure 150 meters radius. 666 meter intervals between structures. 5 miles is 12 intervals. 33966 meters between major settlements along roads/paths. There should be a creek, river or drainage ditch ~666m from the 150m…</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1852529953381797939\">https://x.com/i/status/1852529953381797939</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DrGregLittle2/status/1852529953381797939\">https://x.com/DrGregLittle2/status/1852529953381797939</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1852929874060878051</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1852929874060878051\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-11-03T04:24:42Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1852931049476456825":{"a":"<p>@DrGregLittle2 @lukecaverns I use Google Earth pro desktop and draw circles of 666m and 33966m and then look around the perimeter. Often there might be a ~40m buffer zone between the 33966m interval. Kind of a neutral zone between cities.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1852929874060878051\">https://x.com/i/status/1852929874060878051</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1852931049476456825</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1852931049476456825\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-11-03T04:29:22Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1852932340839813142":{"a":"<p>@DrGregLittle2 @lukecaverns I&#x27;ve not done an extensive amount of looking but it appears that West East axis is parallel to the equator. North South tends to be offset about 6.7 degrees East as you go South.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1852931049476456825\">https://x.com/i/status/1852931049476456825</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1852932340839813142</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1852932340839813142\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-11-03T04:34:30Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1853175380133527966":{"a":"<p>@DrGregLittle2 @lukecaverns Cement and gravel quarries. 1.42 nautical miles (2630m) from those you&#x27;ll usually find a cemetery. The quarries often become a park later on. So check around those as well. Easiest way to make sure no one tries to build someone in a place is to make it a cemetery or park. 😜😳</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1852932340839813142\">https://x.com/i/status/1852932340839813142</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1853175380133527966</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1853175380133527966\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-11-03T20:40:15Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1853176850723340401":{"a":"<p>RT @Scholar_Melinda: First flames started with medicine &amp; carried with grass bundles 🔥🌿 #goodfire #wildfire #Indigenous #NativeTwitter  ty…</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1853176850723340401\">https://x.com/i/status/1853176850723340401</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1853176850723340401</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1853176850723340401\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-11-03T20:46:06Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>retweet</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</d